# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./xymon-plugin at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
# An example of a client part too: see CONTRIBUTING.md, which part where.
name: clientage
version: 0.1.0
summary: the age of a Xymon client's last message, as a column of its host: green, yellow when late, red when much later
manual: clientage.8

# How ./xymon-plugin installs it: see xymonapi's PLUGIN file. On a
# monitored host, a standalone client or a Xymon server's own client tree.
client-short: the clientage column of this host, from its client's last message
client-files: clientage-client.sh
client-manual: clientage.8
client-task: clientage-client.tasks
executable: clientage-client.sh
